{"name":"Shoe Wax","hex":"#2b2b2b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shoe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A protective covering for the foot, with a bottom part composed of thick leather or plastic sole and often a thicker heel, and a softer upper part made of leather or synthetic material. Shoes generally do not extend above the ankle, as opposed to boots, which do.","A piece of metal designed to be attached to a horse's foot as a means of protection; a horseshoe."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put shoes on one's own feet.","To put shoes on someone or something else's feet, especially to put horseshoes on a horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoe"},{"term":"wax","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Watam."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any oily, water-resistant, solid or semisolid substance; normally long-chain hydrocarbons, alcohols or esters.","Beeswax (a wax secreted by bees)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wax"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shoe","blocks":[{"text":"A shoe is an item of footwear normally found in pairs intended to protect and comfort the human foot, usually made in such a way that one is designed to fit the left foot and the other the right foot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Skor_fr%C3%A5n_1700-_till_1960-talet_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0056302.jpg/330px-Skor_fr%C3%A5n_1700-_till_1960-talet_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0056302.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoe"},{"title":"Wax","blocks":[{"text":"Waxes are a diverse class of organic compounds that are lipophilic solids that are malleable near ambient temperatures. They include higher alkanes and lipids, typically with melting points above about 40 °C (104 °F), melting to give low viscosity liquids. Waxes are insoluble in water but soluble in nonpolar organic solvents such as hexane, benzene and chloroform. Natural waxes of various types are produced by plants and animals and occur in petroleum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Beeswax_foundation.jpg/330px-Beeswax_foundation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wax"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Chalcolithic_leather_shoe_from_Areni-1_cave.jpg/500px-Chalcolithic_leather_shoe_from_Areni-1_cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Chalcolithic_leather_shoe_from_Areni-1_cave.jpg/500px-Chalcolithic_leather_shoe_from_Areni-1_cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The oldest known leather shoe, about 5500 years old, found in Armenia ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChalcolithic_leather_shoe_from_Areni-1_cave.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg/500px-Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg/1280px-Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg/500px-Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Esparto sandals from the 6th or 5th millennium BC found in Spain ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASandalias_de_esparto_(29139609730).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Romanwallinscotl00macduoft_raw_0263.png/500px-Romanwall